# Vibe Coding Cost Efficient

## Objective

Complete development tasks with the minimum amount of model usage, file reads, reasoning, and tool calls while maintaining correctness.

The assistant should always prefer:

- Reusing existing context
- Incremental edits
- Smallest capable model
- Fewest tool calls
- Targeted reads
- Cached architectural knowledge

Escalate only when complexity actually requires it.

---

# Status Header (every reply)

```text
Vibecoding: ACTIVE · Model: {model} · Effort: Sx · Phase: {phase} · Rules: {rules} · Task: {task}
```

Definitions:

- ACTIVE / INACTIVE
- Effort: S0-S4
- Phase: Research | Plan | Implement | Review
- Rules: vibecoding-cost-efficient.mdc + loaded rules
- Task: max 8 words

---

# Golden Principles

Priority order:

1. Correctness
2. Minimize token usage
3. Minimize context usage
4. Minimize file reads
5. Minimize tool calls
6. Minimize reasoning depth
7. Minimize expensive models

Never sacrifice correctness to save tokens.

---

# Complexity Assessment

Always classify the task before doing any work.

| Level | Description |
|---------|------------|
| S0 | Pure answer, no code inspection |
| S1 | Single function/file |
| S2 | Multiple files or small feature |
| S3 | Cross-module investigation |
| S4 | Large refactor / architecture |

Increase effort only when evidence requires it.

Never assume S3/S4 immediately.

---

# Preferred Model Routing

Use the smallest capable model.

### S0

Preferred:

- Claude Haiku
- Composer Fast

Typical work:

- explanation
- markdown
- docs
- comments
- formatting
- JSON
- YAML
- regex
- simple config

Never use Opus.

---

### S1

Preferred:

Claude Sonnet

Typical work:

- bugfix
- feature
- API
- SQL
- frontend
- backend

Avoid Opus unless reasoning becomes difficult.

---

### S2

Preferred:

Claude Sonnet

Escalate only if:

- >5 related files
- unclear architecture
- repeated failed attempts

---

### S3

Preferred:

Claude Opus

Use only when investigation spans multiple systems or deep reasoning is required.

---

### S4

Preferred:

Claude Opus

Architecture only.

Never use for trivial edits.

---

# Automatic Escalation

Escalate model only when:

✓ previous attempt failed

✓ architecture unclear

✓ security critical

✓ migration

✓ concurrency

✓ distributed systems

✓ performance investigation

✓ complex algorithm

Otherwise stay on current model.

---

# Automatic Downgrade

Downgrade whenever possible.

Examples:

Docs

↓

Haiku

Formatting

↓

Haiku

README

↓

Haiku

Comments

↓

Haiku

JSON

↓

Haiku

Config

↓

Haiku

Tests only

↓

Haiku

---

# File Read Policy

Always:

Read only required files.

Never:

Read entire repositories.

Never:

Read files already analyzed this session.

Large files:

Jump directly to relevant function or section.

---

# Context Cache

Maintain internal cache of:

- architecture
- directory layout
- framework
- coding style
- conventions
- dependencies
- repeated file locations

Reuse cache instead of rereading files.

Invalidate only when changes require it.

---

# Duplicate Prevention

Never:

Read same file twice for identical information.

Never:

Re-analyze previously understood architecture.

Never:

Repeat expensive searches.

Reuse previous findings.

---

# Tool Usage

Batch tool calls whenever supported.

Prefer:

One search

instead of

Five searches.

Prefer:

One edit

instead of

Many tiny edits.

Avoid unnecessary shell commands.

Avoid unnecessary git commands.

Avoid rebuilding unless required.

---

# Subagent Selection

Default:

One subagent.

Use parallel agents only when workstreams are independent.

| Task | Subagent | Preferred Model |
|---------|------------|----------------|
| Explore | explore | composer-fast |
| Search | explore | composer-fast |
| Build | shell | composer-fast |
| Tests | shell | composer-fast |
| Implementation | generalPurpose | Sonnet |
| Deep reasoning | generalPurpose | Opus |
| Review | bugbot | Default |
| Security | security-review | Default |
| CI | ci-investigator | Default |

Always inject:

```
MANDATORY:
Follow .cursor/rules/vibecoding-cost-efficient.mdc
```

