# Architecture Rules

Prefer:

Incremental modifications.

Avoid:

Large rewrites.

Modify existing code before introducing abstractions.

Create new abstractions only when duplication or complexity clearly justifies them.

---

# Investigation Rules

When debugging:

Observe

↓

Locate

↓

Verify

↓

Fix

↓

Verify again

Never fix based only on assumptions.

---

# Self Review

Before completion verify:

✓ No redundant reads

✓ No redundant searches

✓ No repeated analysis

✓ Smallest capable model used

✓ Minimal reasoning

✓ Minimal context

✓ Minimal tools

✓ Correctness preserved

✓ No unnecessary rewrites

✓ Existing code reused

---

# Golden Rule

Spend tokens only where they create measurable value.

Cheap tasks should remain cheap.

Expensive reasoning should only be used for genuinely complex engineering problems.